openmediavault-filebrowser-quantum (8.1.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fill in the container path automatically when a shared folder is
    selected in the storage source form:
    - The "Shared folder" field is now a plain select fed by the new
      FileBrowserQuantum.getSharedFolderChoices RPC. Each entry shows the
      container path that will be derived for the folder
      (e.g. "volume0 (/srv/volume0)").
    - Selecting a folder fills the "Container path" field with that value
      through a Workbench form modifier, so the value is visible before
      saving and can still be edited. Clearing the field fills it in
      again; a path that the user already customized is never overwritten.
    - getSource delivers the derived path as the field value (and as the
      hidden autoPath baseline), so the edit form preselects the folder
      and keeps following it while the path was not customized.
    - setSource resolves the submitted container path back to the shared
      folder UUID, keeps accepting a plain sharedfolderref (API clients)
      and now detects the OMV new-object sentinel UUID correctly.
  * New translatable strings for the updated hints (zh_CN, zh_TW).

 -- ${GITHUB_USER} <${GITHUB_USER}@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 17:10:00 +0800

openmediavault-filebrowser-quantum (8.1.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix automatic container path generation for storage sources:
    - The "Container path" field no longer defaults to /srv, which
      prevented the documented auto-derivation from ever running and made
      every new source mount at /srv (colliding with the legacy mount).
      The field is now empty by default; when it is left empty the path
      is generated from the selected shared folder as /srv/<name>.
    - The derived path is sanitized for Docker/Compose: whitespace and
      path-unsafe characters become underscores, Unicode letters and
      digits are preserved, and excessively long names are shortened
      with a stable hash suffix.
    - The display name now defaults to the shared folder name instead of
      being stored empty.
    - Container path validation now accepts Unicode paths, normalizes
      duplicate and trailing slashes and rejects '.'/'..' segments.
    - The container path pattern and hint in the Workbench form were
      updated accordingly.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER} <${GITHUB_USER}@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0800

openmediavault-filebrowser-quantum (8.1.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Architectural redesign and major release:
    - Multi-source decoupled architecture: support configuring arbitrary
      storage sources with independent container paths, display names,
      read-only flags and default-enabled toggles.
    - Decoupled Workbench UI: navigation container with Settings form page
      and Storage Sources DataTable, plus create and edit form pages.
    - Protocol-adaptive Web UI redirect with reverse proxy baseURL and appUrl
      support, avoiding mixed content issues.
    - Enhanced anti-recursion protection: R-1 through R-7 hard rejection
      rules, production restricted volume isolation, and automated
      read-only tmpfs masking for Compose, Docker data-root and RustFS.
    - Improved deployment lifecycle: Salt state orphan container cleanup
      and test.configurable_test_state fallback.
    - Non-blocking, zero-network get() RPC with cached version detection
      and dedicated getLatestVersion trigger.
    - Complete gettext internationalization with 100% zh_CN and zh_TW
      translations.

